From 40c9bacdc5a2d780ebfd822b2f8e1fdca601c6c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:35:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/69] HIP FA: RDNA3 kernel reading the q4_0 KV cache directly
 for small batches

For q4_0 K/V and up to 8 tokens, process tokens x GQA heads of a K/V head as
one flattened set of Q columns (tiles of 16) in a single pass over the compact
K/V data with WMMA, instead of the vector kernel (one Q head per block, K/V
re-read per head) or the tile kernel (full-cache f16 conversion every call).
K is dequantized straight into WMMA A fragments, V into a transposed f16 tile
in shared memory; the KV sequence is split across blocks and merged with
flash_attn_combine_results.

Qwen3.8-27B (24 Q / 4 KV heads, D 256), q4_0 KV, per layer at kv 32768:
n=1 236 -> 60 us, n=5 913 -> 111 us, n=8 914 -> 151 us (test-backend-ops).
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/fattn-kvq.cu  | 645 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/fattn-kvq.cuh |   8 +
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/fattn.cu      |  11 +
 tests/test-backend-ops.cpp       |  16 +
 4 files changed, 680 insertions(+)
